# Agent skills. `npx skills add` always installs project skills into
# .agents/skills/<name>, so they are ignored by default and skills-lock.json is
# what records them. Skills authored here are allowlisted: add a line for each
# new one (tests/test_skills_gitignore.py checks it).
/.agents/skills/*
!/.agents/skills/cli-subagents/
!/.agents/skills/development-best-practices/
!/.agents/skills/finding-high-value-reading/
!/.agents/skills/macos-disk-cleanup/
!/.agents/skills/macos-kernel-task-cpu/
!/.agents/skills/mojo/
!/.agents/skills/okf/
!/.agents/skills/portfolio/
!/.agents/skills/python-styleguide/
!/.agents/skills/ranking-llms-by-benchmark/
